Spec: Protocol/Symbols

Purpose:
  Token-efficient, machine-readable status vocabulary for .sdd files.
  Symbols replace verbose state words (e.g. PROCESS_DONE -> +).

Forbids:
  Using these symbols inside actual source code comments.
  (They are AI-oriented metadata for .sdd files only — a developer reading
  source code gains nothing from "// +" the way they would from a real
  comment; keep source code comments normal.)

Vocabulary:
  +  = DONE / PASS
  -  = FAIL
  ~  = IN_PROGRESS / ACTIVE
  !  = BLOCKED
  ?  = NEED_INPUT / DECISION
  >  = NEXT
  @  = REFERENCE
  #  = RULE

ProgressNotation:
  Fractional form (N of M subtasks done):
    ~ 2/5

  Stage form (which stage is currently active, others pending/done):
    + BE, ~ FE, ? QA

Example:
  backend.module.design ~     (in progress)
  backend.module.design +     (done)
  backend.module.design -     (failed)
  > backend.ddd                (next skill/stage to run)

Reference:
  Stage abbreviations used alongside these symbols (AN, AR, DB, BE, API,
  FE, MD, QA, DO, VR) are defined in protocol/stages.sdd, not here — this
  file is the state/status vocabulary only.
